{
  "meta": {
    "comment": [
      "SPDX-FileCopyrightText: \u00a9 2026 Christopher Woods <Christopher.Woods@bristol.ac.uk>",
      "SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0",
      "",
      "Synthetic `sacct --json --duplicates --allocations` output, shaped like real",
      "output from a production Slurm but carrying no real project's data. Every",
      "record covers a window of one day: 2026-03-01T00:00:00Z (1772323200) to",
      "2026-03-02T00:00:00Z (1772409600).",
      "",
      "Nodes are all `testnode`, which the tests map to a 128-cpu, 128-billing node,",
      "so a job allocating the whole node bills one node-second per second and the",
      "expected values are the elapsed times themselves. A node name the test's",
      "`SlurmNodes` does not know would silently fall back to the default node and",
      "change every number here - see the anonymisation note in",
      "docs/plans/slurm-requeue-accounting-design.md.",
      "",
      "The cases, in order:",
      "  100 - never requeued. One record, the whole of it inside the window.",
      "  200 - requeued once, both attempts inside the window. Attempt 0 was",
      "        preempted after 3600s; attempt 1 completed in 1800s.",
      "  300 - requeued twice, all three attempts inside the window. The two",
      "        superseded attempts were node failures, on named nodes.",
      "  400 - earlier attempts fell before the window, so the lowest restart_cnt",
      "        returned is 2, not 0. Tests that classification orders attempts",
      "        rather than looking for restart_cnt == 0.",
      "  500 - the final attempt was cancelled before it ran, so it has zero",
      "        elapsed. Everything this job consumed belongs to the requeue bucket",
      "        and its base usage is zero - which is what we reported before,",
      "        because the zero-elapsed record was the only one sacct returned.",
      "  600 - two unrelated jobs sharing an id after a job-id reset: two records,",
      "        both with restart_cnt 0. Neither may be classed as a requeue of the",
      "        other.",
      "  700 - an attempt that started before the window and was requeued inside",
      "        it, so its usage is clipped but its start is outside.",
      "  800 - a state Slurm reports that TERMINAL_STATES does not name, which must",
      "        be bucketed as OTHER rather than dropped.",
      "  900 - the shape almost every real requeue has, and the one that made the",
      "        first version of the event count useless. A long attempt starts on",
      "        day one, runs past midnight and is requeued on day two; the attempt",
      "        that replaces it is cancelled before it runs, so it has zero elapsed.",
      "        The two records only ever appear in one response together in the",
      "        day-two window, which is where the requeue must be counted - the",
      "        attempt's own start is on day one. Spans the second window,",
      "        2026-03-02T00:00:00Z (1772409600) to 2026-03-03T00:00:00Z",
      "        (1772496000)."
    ]
  },
